# The key findings include:

Students with higher attendance levels consistently achieve higher scores.
Increased study hours show a positive correlation with overall academic performance.
Students with adequate sleep patterns demonstrate better academic outcomes compared to those with sleep deprivation.
These insights help demonstrate how lifestyle and study habits contribute to academic performance.

## Student Lifestyle & Behavioral Insights

Moderate stress levels appear associated with balanced performance, while very high stress correlates with lower scores.
Students maintaining healthy sleep patterns tend to achieve stronger academic results.
Participation in activities may positively contribute to overall engagement and performance.

## Socioeconomic Impact on Academic Outcomes

This section examines external factors affecting student success.
Students whose parents have higher levels of education often achieve higher academic scores.
Internet access at home shows a positive association with academic performance, highlighting the role of digital resources in education.
Family background variables can influence opportunities and learning environments.


# Key Takeaway

This project demonstrates how data visualization and analytics can uncover meaningful insights in educational data, 
helping educators and institutions better understand factors that influence student performance.
